# Upstream Brief Workflow

## When to Use

- The user invokes `/upstream-brief`.
- The user wants official-docs research so agent instructions stop teaching a stale API.
- The user names one or more languages, frameworks, or libraries plus target versions.

## Core Approach

Read and follow `.github/skills/upstream-brief/SKILL.md` exactly.

- Human names each `subject@version`. The adapter resolves current versions. Never fetch “latest.”
- One user-invoked skill. Parallelism is Independent Hops (one research worker per subject).
- Write one Upstream Brief. Apply no instruction, script, or application-code edits.
- Findings need a primary upstream citation for the named target.
- Proposed plan = repo-owned instructions and hygiene scripts. Application code and vendor-skill pins are follow-on.
- Propose a HITL issue only when there is a finding; file only on confirm. Do not start a grill.

## Skill Files

- `.github/skills/upstream-brief/SKILL.md`
- `.github/skills/upstream-brief/ADAPTER.md`
- `.github/skills/upstream-brief/BRIEF.md`
- `upstream-brief.config.yml`
- `docs/adr/0018-upstream-brief-portable-instruction-audit.md`
